timeline.body:
should this be `isAuthorizedAndAvailable` ? If we are prescriptive in the names, i think the names should match with their expectations for implementations and be consistent with each other.  

However, I do prefer interface names to be less prescriptive so that implementors have more freedom to deviate but still adhere to the interface. For example, if the name were more generic then the same interface could be used to get all authorized but *un*avaible 

So my actual preference would be for this interface to be something like the following
 
```java
interface AuthorizedIndices {
   //javdoc here
   Supplier<Set<String>> all();
  //javadoc here
   boolean check(String name);
}
```
So usage would read:
```
authorizedIndices.all().get();
authorizedIndices.check("foo");
```

